<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="575165b9">A work breakdown structure (WBS) is a deliverable oriented decomposition of a project into smaller components. It defines
and groups a project&apos;s discrete work elements in a way that helps organize and define the total work scope of the project.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="4253e92a"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="89571740">This can be captured as an outline is MS Word or more formally in a specialized WBS modeling tool such as WBS
Schedule Pro or with a sophisticated project planning tool such as Primavera.  In some cases these are referred to as
a &quot;WBS Dictionary&quot;.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="9e6963dc"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="2a8bb0cc">To define discrete work elements in a way that helps organize and define the total work scope of the project.</attribute>
